### Using Cubit in UI
```dart
// Screen receives Cubit from router - NO manual instantiation
class UserScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const UserScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    // Cubit is already provided by BlocProvider in app_router.dart
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('User Profile')),
      body: BlocConsumer<UserCubit, UserState>(
        listener: (context, state) {
          state.whenOrNull(
            error: (message) => ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
              SnackBar(content: Text(message)),
            ),
          );
        },
        builder: (context, state) {
          return state.when(
            initial: () => const SizedBox.shrink(),
            loading: () => const Center(child: CircularProgressIndicator()),
            loaded: (user) => _buildUserContent(context, user),
            loadedList: (users) => _buildUserList(users),
            error: (message) => Center(
              child: Column(
                mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
                children: [
                  Text(message),
                  const SizedBox(height: 16),
                  ElevatedButton(
                    onPressed: () => context.read<UserCubit>().loadUser('user123'),
                    child: const Text('Retry'),
                  ),
                ],
              ),
            ),
          );
        },
      ),
    );
  }

  Widget _buildUserContent(BuildContext context, User user) {
    return Padding(
      padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),
      child: Column(
        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,
        children: [
          Text('Name: ${user.name}'),
          Text('Email: ${user.email}'),
          const SizedBox(height: 20),
          ElevatedButton(
            onPressed: () {
              final updatedUser = user.copyWith(name: 'New Name');
              context.read<UserCubit>().updateUser(updatedUser);
            },
            child: const Text('Update User'),
          ),
          const SizedBox(height: 10),
          ElevatedButton(
            onPressed: () {
              // Navigate to edit screen with data
              context.push('/edit-user', extra: user);
            },
            child: const Text('Edit User'),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }

  Widget _buildUserList(List<User> users) {
    return ListView.builder(
      itemCount: users.length,
      itemBuilder: (context, index) {
        final user = users[index];
        return ListTile(
          title: Text(user.name),
          subtitle: Text(user.email),
          onTap: () => context.go('/user/${user.id}'),
        );
      },
    );
  }
}
```

## Additional Instructions for AI Agents

**CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE RULES (MVVM):**
- **Follow MVVM pattern STRICTLY** - only `data/` and `presentation/` folders in features
- **NO domain layer, NO use cases** - all business logic goes directly in Cubits
- **Cubit = ViewModel** - contains all business logic, validation, and data transformation
- **Repository = Model** - only handles data fetching/caching, no business logic
- **Widgets = View** - only UI and user interaction, delegates all logic to Cubit

**CRITICAL DEPENDENCY INJECTION RULES (GetIt):**
- **NEVER manually instantiate** repositories, data sources, or Cubits
- **ALWAYS use GetIt** for dependency injection: `getIt<ClassName>()`
- **Register data sources and repositories as lazy singletons** in injection.dart
- **Register Cubits as factories** (not singletons) so each route gets a fresh instance
- **Inject dependencies via constructor** - never use service locator pattern inside classes
- **Setup GetIt in main.dart** before running the app

**CRITICAL ROUTING RULES (GoRouter):**
- **ALL navigation must use GoRouter** - never use Navigator.push or MaterialPageRoute
- **Define all routes in app_router.dart** - single source of truth for routing
- **Provide Cubits at route level** in app_router.dart using BlocProvider
- **Inject Cubits using GetIt** in the route builder: `getIt<UserCubit>()`
- **Never create BlocProvider inside screens** - always in app_router.dart
- Use `context.go()` for navigation, `context.push()` for stacking, `context.pop()` for back
- Pass data using `extra` parameter or path/query parameters

**CRITICAL STATE MANAGEMENT RULES:**
- **ALWAYS use Cubit** for state management (never Provider, Riverpod, GetX, or other solutions)
- **ALWAYS use Either from dartz** for error handling in repositories
- **NEVER use Result, Try, or other error handling patterns** - only Either<Failure, Success>
- **NEVER create UseCase classes** - Cubits call repositories directly

**CUBIT RESPONSIBILITY (ViewModel):**
- Data validation (email format, required fields, etc.)
- Business rules (age limits, calculation logic, etc.)
- Data transformation (formatting, filtering, sorting)
- Calling repositories to fetch/save data (injected via GetIt)
- Mapping failures to user-friendly messages
- Managing UI state (loading, success, error)

**REPOSITORY RESPONSIBILITY (Model):**
- Fetching data from API/Database
- Caching data locally
- Handling data sources (remote/local)
- Returning Either<Failure, Data>
- NO business logic, NO validation

**SCREEN RESPONSIBILITY (View):**
- Display UI and handle user interactions
- Read Cubit from context (never create it): `context.read<UserCubit>()`
- Listen to state changes using BlocBuilder/BlocListener/BlocConsumer
- Navigate using GoRouter: `context.go()`, `context.push()`
- NO business logic, NO direct repository access

